.TH MX-USB-UNMOUNTER 1 "2026-07-20" "MX Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx-usb-unmounter \- unmount removable devices from the system tray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx-usb-unmounter
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx-usb-unmounter
runs in the system tray and provides an action window for unmounting USB storage, MTP devices, GPhoto2 devices, and optical discs. Left-click the tray icon to open the action window. Double-clicking an entry unmounts it.
.PP
Right-click the tray icon for the device list, help, about information, and quit commands. Notifications report whether an unmount operation succeeds or fails. Close the action window by clicking outside it, pressing Escape, or selecting Cancel. Hover over a device to view its mount point.
.PP
Only one instance runs for a user at a time.
.SH OPTIONS
This application has no documented command-line options. The graphical interface and system tray menu provide all operations.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mx-usb-unmounter
Installed HTML help, images, license, and changelog documentation.
.SH AUTHOR
MX Linux contributors.
